# Used by: docker build -f sethucms/docker/Dockerfile.gateway ...
# The build context is the folder that holds all the repositories, so without this file
# Docker would copy your own node_modules, built output and local data into the image.
# That breaks the install (host links are not valid in the container) and, worse, could
# bake local databases, tokens and .env files into an image you later publish.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.git
**/.github
**/.sethucms-data
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.log
**/.next
**/coverage
**/.turbo
